
# Episode 4: The Warehouse Fire

A fire destroyed a warehouse on the industrial waterfront.

Investigators ruled it an accident caused by faulty wiring.

The case seemed simple.

Detective D. Torque wasn't convinced.

The burn patterns didn't match an electrical fire.

Someone had used an accelerant.

Torque examined security footage from nearby businesses.

A masked figure was seen entering the warehouse shortly before the fire began.

Inside the ruins, investigators recovered partially burned documents.

Most were destroyed.

One survived.

The document contained shipping records connected to Hale Industries.

The warehouse had been storing evidence.

Someone wanted it gone.

Following financial records, Torque discovered payments made to the warehouse manager.

The manager admitted he had been paid to leave a side entrance unlocked.

The masked figure was identified and arrested.

The fire had been planned to destroy evidence before authorities could find it.

Case Closed.

Among the recovered documents was the same mysterious symbol.

Now the connection between the cases could no longer be ignored.
